            <ArticleTitle>Kombucha: is a cup of tea good for you?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr-2017-221702</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2017-221702</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 54-year-old asthmatic woman presented to hospital with a 10-day history of breathlessness. On examination, she was tachypnoeic with mild wheeze. She had preserved peak flows and was saturating at 100% on room air. Investigations revealed severe metabolic lactic acidosis. On further questioning, it transpired that she drank kombucha tea, which has been linked to lactic acidosis. She made a full recovery with supportive management and cessation of the tea.</AbstractText>
